course: dictionary
lesson: 12153
title: Words about ability
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how well someone can do something. Competence is one of them. It means the ability to do something well enough, or properly. «Sara showed competence when she fixed the bike chain on her own.» She knew what to do and did it well, so she showed competence.
explain: Competence is an uncountable noun, so we do not say "a competence" for the general idea. We say "competence in reading" or "competence with tools". Schools use the word in reports, such as «Tom's competence in maths is good this term.»
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Only competent people may use the saw» tells you that a competent person is someone who can use it safely and properly. Check your meaning by swapping it in: "Only people who can use it well may use the saw" still makes sense, so you are right.
fact: Competence means the ability to do something well enough or properly.
fact: «Competence» is uncountable, so you say «competence in reading», not «a competence» for the general idea.
fact: In a formal sense, a competence is a skill someone has, such as «core competences» needed for a job or course.
fact: In law, «competence» means being able to make decisions for yourself.
fact: Do not mix up «competence» with «confidence»: confidence is believing in yourself, while competence is being able to do the task well.
exercise: «Sara showed competence when she fixed the bike chain on her own.» What does competence mean here? | Asking someone else to do it | Feeling nervous about the task | Being very fast at running | *Being able to do the job well
exercise: «Her ___ in swimming means she can swim well.» Which word fits best? | Curiosity | *Competence | Cruelty | Celebration
exercise: Which sentence uses competence correctly? | «Her competence is a happy dog.» | «She ran competence home.» | «The competence was blue.» | *«Her competence with tools is excellent.»
test: «Only competent people may use the saw.» What does competent mean? | Very tired | Able to run very fast | Very loud | *Able to do it well and safely
test: In law, what does «competence» mean? | *Being able to make decisions for yourself | Owning a house | Being famous | Being very tall
exam: Which word means the ability to do something well enough? | celebration | cruelty | *competence | curiosity
